cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bounds on K(8,1,2), the first unknown term of OEIS A004045"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hanyu
    family-names: Yang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0419-4070"
abstract: >-
  Artifacts for lower bounds on binary multiple covering codes. An elementary
  parity/excess argument shows that for even n every binary code whose closed
  radius-1 balls cover each point at least twice satisfies
  |C| >= ceil(3 * 2^(n+1) / (3n+2)). This strictly improves the best published
  lower bound on K(n,1,2) at n = 8, 10, 12, 14 and 16, and reproves the exact
  value K(6,1,2) = 20 without computer search. In particular K(8,1,2) >= 60,
  one above the published lower bound, established by three independent routes.
  The package also contains a candidate refutation of |C| = 60 that would give
  K(8,1,2) >= 61, machine-checkable certificates, and a Lean 4 formalisation.
keywords:
  - covering codes
  - multiple covering codes
  - Hamming space
  - OEIS A004045
  - double domination
  - hypercube
  - Delsarte inequalities
  - Lean 4
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SeverinVisionary/oeis-a004045"
references:
